{
  "_about": "VolumeRoute.of: THE VOLUME-SAFETY RULE. On an Android TV a volume key never goes out as a protocol key unless the launcher is known to be absent (known == false); with a launcher, or not knowing yet, it goes through POST /volume (launcher-6470/volume-outcome.json decides what happens then). A protocol volume key reboots the SHIELD (Android 11) while GoatLauncher watches the keys: incidents c06672a, bcc9ca4, b272212. A TV that reports no volume control gets an explanation instead. Every entry point (tap, hold, hardware buttons, Shortcuts) goes through it. Written from the behaviour before the move (VM/RM at origin/parity 3183ca9). Android data/Policies.kt and RemoteCore Policies.swift must both pass every row.",
